<title>INDIA: India's RBI removes CRR on inter-bank borrowings.</title>
<headline>India's RBI removes CRR on inter-bank borrowings.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India on Tuesday removed the cash reserve ratio requirement (CRR) on inter-bank borrowings in its monetary policy for the first half of 1997/98 (April-March).  </p>
<p>The new rule is effective from the fortnight beginning April 26, 1997, the central bank said.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
